gen() { printf "%s" "$2" | higgsfield generate create gpt_image_2 --aspect_ratio 16:9 --resolution 1k --wait --json > "$1.json" 2>&1; }
gen dispatch "Desktop website first-viewport UI design mockup, 1440x810, flat screen render, no device frame. Personal portfolio of a software engineer styled as a live taxi-dispatch control console. Committed palette: saturated taxi-yellow (#FFC400) field covering half the screen, jet-black ink, off-white panels, one signal green for LIVE status. Left half: huge condensed grotesque headline 'MOHAMED EMAD' in black on yellow, under it 'Software Engineer — builds the whole product: database, API, dashboard, mobile app.' and two buttons 'See shipped work' and 'Download CV'. Right half: a minimal vector map of the Nile valley with a pulsing pin labeled 'Minya, EG' and thin dashed dispatch routes to labels 'Saudi Arabia' and 'United Kingdom'. Bottom strip: a dispatch queue table with rows 'JOB 01 TaxiMatch — Real-time dispatch · LIVE on Google Play', 'JOB 02 Web Creator — Multi-tenant SaaS', 'JOB 03 Ajlcom — Automotive marketplace · LIVE', 'JOB 04 NAA — Education platform · LIVE', monospace status chips. Top nav: 'ME' monogram, Work, Stack, Experience, Contact. Crisp, precise, Swiss-industrial, generous spacing, legible text."
